searchers\nStaff\nInstitutions and companies\nHeader\nLogin\nEN\nIT\nToggle language menu\nSearch\nPh.D. programme in Chemical Engineering\nSkip to main content\nAcademic Board\nCareer opportunities\nStudy plan\nResearch topics\nAdvisory Board\nRegulations\nStudents\nAlumni\nBreadcrumb\nHome\nEducation\nPh.D. programmes and Postgraduate School\nPh.D. programmes\nChemical Engineering\nProgramme overview\nImmagine\nThe PhD programme in Chemical Engineering aims at training highly-qualified professionals with a focus on promoting innovation in the field of chemical engineering and process engineering.\nThe training process is developed on two fronts. On the one hand, it comprises a teaching part, in which courses are taught traditionally and course load can be personalized on the basis of each student\u2019s needs, such as to fill any scientific and cultural gaps.\nAcquiring the mentality and methodologies required to foster innovation is a goal achievable by means of focused studies on process and products innovation. PhD students are not only supervised by their tutor, but they also have the opportunity to engage in an exchange of ideas with other members of Academic Board.\nConcerning the modalities of courses attendance, usually students shall acquire basic knowledge and competences during the first year, while also deciding what will be their research topic, under their tutor\u2019s supervision. In the second year they shall focus on research activity and taking part to specialized seminars. Between second and third year, a term is often spent abroad, studying and researching at other universities or research centres, in order to further develop their research.\nGo to the call for applications\nKey information\nType of programme:\nPhD programme\nDepartment:\nDepartment of Applied Science and Technology\nCoordinator:\nPISANO ROBERTO\nVice coordinator:\nSIMONE ELENA\nAdmissions:\nOpen, through competitive selection\nTitolo\nContacts\nContatti e-mail\nTitolo\nStudent